From ea2611bc59cb558511a8f4cfd85aaf7a45c8296d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Braden <snufflyy@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:38:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: batch engine draws, cache geometry in VRAM, no
 per-frame readback

Every engine draw was its own command buffer, submitted and waited on,
because all draws shared one vertex buffer, constant buffer and
descriptor set. On SARPBC 01.09's menus (~150-190 draws a frame) the
FIFO thread sat in vkWaitForFences for every draw.

- Draws record into one open command buffer, each with its own slice
  of per-batch vertex/index/constant arenas and its own descriptor set,
  ordered by a memory barrier. The batch is submitted by anything else
  that needs the GPU (vk_begin: uploads, clears, readbacks, present),
  by any destroy, and by the engine's submit_and_wait, so everything
  outside it keeps the "complete on return" contract.
  PS3RECOMP_VK_BATCH=0 submits after each draw again.
- Vertex and index data go through a 64 MB content cache (128-bit hash
  of the bytes) in device-local, host-visible memory when there is
  some: data drawn before is not uploaded again. Menus pass ~38 KB of
  vertices+indices per draw, mostly the same every frame; read from
  host memory a draw cost 30-70 us of GPU time (1.2 ms for a 7.8k-vertex
  mesh) on a PCIe 2.0 x4 link. PS3RECOMP_VK_GEO_CACHE=0 disables it.
- Unchanged constants reuse the previous draw's slice in the batch (69%
  of the 8 KB vertex-constant binds are unchanged).
- On the engine path, present reads nothing back unless a frame dump is
  due (the engine answers readback_center itself); test case added.
- Diagnostics: PS3RECOMP_VK_BATCH_STATS=1 (draws per batch, GPU wait
  time), PS3RECOMP_VK_DRAW_TIMES=1 (GPU timestamps per draw).

SARPBC 01.09 Choose Profile screen, PS3_VERBOSE=0, same machine:
~23 fps -> 32.5 fps, identical frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
